        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "Correct me if I’m wrong, but Omarchy is just an Arch installer + a Hyprland rice + DHH’s favorite apps preinstalled.\n\nHow is that better than grabbing a solid rice from r/unixporn and asking an AI to set it up?\n\nThey’re selling the “AI-first OS” angle hard, yet AI can already debug, install packages and configure systems on any Linux distro. Nothing unique there.\n\nAnd the big claim about preventing the classic “update broke my system” problem? \nThey’re relying on Btrfs/Snapper snapshots (the same approach openSUSE has used for years)… while NixOS (a real OS btw) solved it more comprehensively with atomic generations.\n\nIs there actually something substantial here, or is it mostly hype?"
        },
